// FROZEN — pennsync-oasis-response-v1-legacy.
//
// ██ DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE ██
//
// This is a byte-faithful snapshot of the response sets PennSync used BEFORE the
// CMS-aligned cutover, captured from `oasisQuestions.jsx` at commit
// 3348e157290d2ead3b904f96b0bb017f4caa2d67. It exists for exactly one purpose:
// so a response saved under the old meanings can still be DISPLAYED with the
// label it was actually answered under.
//
// Editing it would retroactively change what a stored answer means, which is the
// precise failure this whole cutover exists to prevent. Adding an item here is
// equally wrong: the snapshot is closed. If a legacy label is wrong, it is still
// what the clinician saw, and the record must keep saying so.
//
// Values are recorded as they were stored — JS NUMBERS, because that is what the
// legacy writer persisted. They are deliberately not normalised to strings: a
// legacy `1` and a v2 `"1"` are different facts and the type difference is part
// of the evidence.
//
// NOTHING in v1 is carryable, exportable with a code, or CMS-scorable. That is
// enforced in `registry.js`, not here — this file only remembers.

